---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Chart from '../components/Chart.astro';
import { asset } from '../lib/paths';
import { monitored, verified, manualCost, ourCost } from '../data/series';
---

<Base>
  <main>
    <section class="hero" id="platform">
      <div class="col">
        <span class="logo" role="img" aria-label="Carbon Valinor" style={`--logo: url(${asset('logo.svg')})`}></span>
        <p data-words>
          <span class="lead" role="heading" aria-level="1">Carbon Valinor builds software for carbon.</span>{' '}
          Every CO₂ storage project generates data from dozens of systems, and most of
          it still ends up in spreadsheets. We pull it into one record and use AI to
          analyse it, so operators know what happened to each tonne.
        </p>
        <p data-words>
          We want permanent storage to be cheap to prove. Once it is, storing carbon
          stops being a last resort and becomes the default.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="monitoring">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Every tonne, accounted for.</span>{' '}
        Our models read wellhead and downhole pressure, fibre-optic sensing,
        time-lapse seismic, satellite data on surface movement and soil-gas
        measurements. They learn how each site normally behaves and monitor it around
        the clock, across <span class="counter" data-keep>1,243,118</span> tonnes so
        far. If pressure drifts, the plume moves somewhere unexpected or two meters
        disagree, the operator gets an alert with the likely cause. We reconcile the
        mass balance from capture to injection and store each reading with a
        timestamp, in formats regulators and registries accept.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="stored"
        series={[
          { label: 'CO₂ monitored', value: '1.24 Mt', data: monitored },
          { label: 'Verified', value: '1.17 Mt', data: verified },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="cost">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Cheaper every year.</span>{' '}
        Monitoring, reporting and verification add real cost to every stored tonne.
        We automate most of that work, so the cost per tonne goes down each year and
        the evidence stays just as strong.
      </p>
      <Chart
        id="cost"
        series={[
          { label: 'Manual, per tonne', value: '$18.40', data: manualCost },
          { label: 'With Carbon Valinor', value: '$4.20', data: ourCost },
        ]}
      />
    </section>

    <section class="col" id="contact">
      <p data-words>
        <span class="lead">Work with us.</span>{' '}
        We work with companies that capture, transport, store or account for CO₂.
        If that’s you, write to us.
      </p>
      <p class="closing" data-words>
        <a class="mail" href="mailto:info@carbonvalinor.com">info@carbonvalinor.com</a>
      </p>
      <footer><span data-words>© 2026 Carbon Valinor</span></footer>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
